From 75475201818ddc21cf8de13b7a63b1ab073bdbb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwen35 <qwen35@local>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 03:09:07 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] [GPU] Token-tiled dispatch for paged_causal_conv1d

At prefill seq_count == 1, so the reference kernel dispatches only `hidden` work-items
({seq_count, hidden}, every work-item walks the whole sequence), which cannot fill the
device's hardware-thread budget. Split each sequence into G contiguous token tiles
(GWS = {seq, hidden, G}); every work-item streams its tile with a sliding window and
primes the K-1 history elements once per tile, so the per-element fma order is identical
to the serial kernel (bit-exact for any G, G == 1 is the original kernel).

G is chosen from the device thread budget (EU * threads/EU, ~1.5x oversubscription),
capped so that tiles stay >= 16 tokens; decode (1 token) falls back to G = 1.
OV_CONV1D_TOKEN_GROUPS=<n> forces G, OV_CONV1D_DEBUG=1 prints the choice once.
